## Fixture 2, "A restored surface": a world-scope plastic Kd 0.1,
## then a block declaring plastic Kd 1.0 around one sphere at x=1.2, then a
## second sphere at x=-1.2 after AttributeEnd, which belongs to the
## restored Kd 0.1 surface. Ks 0 and no ambient light make brightness
## linear in Kd, so a correct render puts the restored sphere's red
## channel near a tenth of the block's. A build that shares one shader
## instance's parameter list across calls would still hold the block's
## Kd 1.0 list when the restored sphere shades, under both renderers.
## Not third-party.
Display "surfaceparameters_restored.tif" "file" "rgba"
Format 200 100 1
Projection "perspective" "fov" [45]
Clipping 0.5 50
Translate 0 0 5
WorldBegin
LightSource "distantlight" 1 "intensity" [1.0] "lightcolor" [1 1 1]
	"from" [0 0 -5] "to" [0 0 0]
Surface "plastic" "Kd" [0.1] "Ks" [0]
AttributeBegin
	Translate 1.2 0 0
	Surface "plastic" "Kd" [1.0] "Ks" [0]
	Sphere 1 -1 1 360
AttributeEnd
Translate -1.2 0 0
Sphere 1 -1 1 360
WorldEnd
